# Backend

This folder holds **application** code for server-side features. AWS wiring lives
in `infra/` (one service → one `.tf` file); the UI stays in `frontend/`.

## Principles

- Add Lambda/API Gateway, containers, or other compute only when a feature needs
  it — not preemptively.
- Validate Cognito JWTs at the API boundary; do not trust client-only checks for
  authorization.
- Secrets via env/SSM/Secrets Manager — never committed. Same GitHub OIDC deploy
  model; extend IAM in Terraform with least privilege.
- Prefer typed handlers, explicit error responses, and shared domain types (mirror
  frontend strict TypeScript where the stack is TS).

## Infra pairing

New backend surface → new or extended module under `infra/modules/`, outputs for
URLs/ARNs, frontend reads public endpoints through `lib/env.ts` if needed.

## Checks

Add CI steps when code exists (lint, test, build/package). Match Node `>=24` if
using TypeScript unless the runtime dictates otherwise.
